\name{cellucid_field_create_from_pages}
\alias{cellucid_field_create_from_pages}
\title{Make a field from highlight pages}
\usage{
cellucid_field_create_from_pages(
  viewer,
  key,
  pages,
  intersection_labels,
  overlap = "first",
  overlap_label = "Overlap",
  uncovered_label = "Unassigned"
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{key}{The new column's name. Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
\item{pages}{The pages, in order (first and last refer to it), each with its category label. A vector or list of a named list (at least 1 item). Required.}
\item{intersection_labels}{With overlap "intersections": the label of each combination of pages that has cells. A vector or list of a named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{overlap}{Cells on several pages: the first page's label, the last's, the overlap label, or one label per combination of pages. One of \code{"first"}, \code{"last"}, \code{"overlap-label"}, \code{"intersections"}. Default \code{"first"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{overlap_label}{The label of cells on several pages when overlap is "overlap-label". Text. Default \code{"Overlap"}, the viewer's own.}
\item{uncovered_label}{The category of cells on no page; empty leaves them without one. Text. Default \code{"Unassigned"}, the viewer's own.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
A new categorical column whose categories are highlight pages: each page's cells take its label; cells on several pages follow the overlap rule.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{field.create-from-pages} (Fields). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labelled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{field-overlays}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_field_create_from_pages(viewer,
      key = "x", pages = list(list(label = "T cells",
          page = "x")))
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
